@startuml 0001-after
!include <C4/C4_Component>

title Work Order Model - After Priority Levels

Component(workorder, "WorkOrder", "Entity", "Enhanced work order model with priority classification")
Component(priority, "WorkOrderPriority", "Enum", "Urgent | High | Normal | Low")

Rel(workorder, priority, "uses")

Rel(workorder, workorder, "Properties:\n- Id: Guid\n- Number: string\n- Title: string\n- Description: string\n- Instructions: string\n- RoomNumber: string\n- **Priority: WorkOrderPriority** (NEW)\n- Status: WorkOrderStatus\n- Creator: Employee\n- Assignee: Employee\n- CreatedDate: DateTime\n- AssignedDate: DateTime\n- CompletedDate: DateTime\n- Attachments: Collection")

note right of priority
  **Priority Levels:**
  - Urgent (Red): Safety hazards, critical failures
  - High (Orange): Important operational issues
  - Normal (Blue): Standard maintenance (default)
  - Low (Gray): Nice-to-have improvements
end note

note left of workorder
  **New Capabilities:**
  ✓ Priority field with enum constraint
  ✓ Default value: Normal
  ✓ Visual indicators (colors/icons)
  ✓ Sort by priority (Urgent first)
  ✓ Filter by priority level
  ✓ Clear prioritization for staff
end note

@enduml
